From 68ad0b6e39084eedc32e28a3755332f2626cc362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:55:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docs(process): bring the PR-reviewer agent up to today's
 review practice

- The agent sets the PR's review label itself (merge-ready / needs-rework /
  conflicts / needs-maintainer, per review-prs step 2b) and removes the
  others, so every reviewed PR is visible on the PR list; a new step 7 says
  how, including our own PRs going back to draft on red or orange.
- Worktrees live under .claude/worktrees/ (AGENTS.md), each with its own
  CARGO_TARGET_DIR; cleanup removes the target too.
- A dispatcher-named per-PR lock (.claude/pr-review-<N>.lock) is honoured
  for side-by-side reviews; only your own lock is ever deleted.
- Builds and tests run in the foreground with a timeout: several reviews
  stalled waiting on background runs that had already died.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
